 "notes": "1-bit photocopy, 2550x3313. Frame on all four sides: thick bar, white hairline, thin inner rule (the innermost rule); the sides bow by up to ~16 px end to end; corner arcs (thick + thin) in all four corners. Outline on paper ~1.5 px inside the thin rule's inner edge (README rules 1, 8); points every <=60 px. Corners (rule 2): the outline follows the inner edge of the thin arc (fitted circles R 117-130 px, residual rms <0.5 px, then measured edge by angle); where an arc meets its side rule through a short stub/joggle the outline steps round it, so stubs stay outside. Kind (b) ink under the outline: hatched and solid commercial blocks run into the top rule (x ~950-2250) and the right rule (y ~1180-1300, 1830-1930), and the outline follows the rule's inner edge through them; at the top-right and bottom-right arcs hatch lines touch the thin arc. Left side y 880-960: a map line runs 1 px inside the thin rule; the outline is put by hand in the 1-2 px paper gap between them (x ~318-319), merging over ~10 px where they touch. remove: (1) the CITY & COUNTY ... USE OF PROPERTY / ZONE MAP title, LEGEND swatches and the 1900 scale bar (top left, floating on blank paper inside the TL arc; no ruled box), a 12-point stepped outline 4-8 px outside the ink, kept clear of THE PORTAL street lines on its right and the hatched blocks below; a small 8x13 px mark at (327-334, 672-684) beside the frame is left as map; (2) the compass rose with true-north needle and arrowhead (top ~584) and the tail feather (down to ~1060): it is printed over the hatching, so the 12-point outline takes the whole rose and crosses hatch lines (that is the remove-outline ink); Mt Davidson lettering stays map; (3) the SECTION 13 badge (ring centre 2327,375, outer radius 34.5), an octagon 5 px outside the ring; it sits on hatched blocks, which it crosses. 'Join Sec. 6/12/14' print outside the frame. Doubt: the 1921 rules are ragged 1-bit edges, so single columns still touch the outline; the BL arc meets the bottom rule through a small stub at x ~425-450, which the outline steps round.",
 "drawn_by": "Claude (test-label agent TA, issue #71), 2026-11-21: from the scan and inputs/frame-labels/README.md only (no model output looked at). Sides: inner edge of the innermost rule measured on every 2nd px along each side from luminance profiles, robust local-linear fit, outline 1.5 px inside the edge (first clean paper row); corner arcs from rays out of a fitted centre (inner edge of the thin arc, smoothed by angle), the region beyond each arc cut away; remove blocks from ink extents / connected components at full resolution. Every flagged vertex and the top-ranked ink stretches checked close up. TEST SET: never train on it."
}
